#
# ============================================================================
#  Kconfig.debug -- EVERY debug/diagnostic knob of the meshtastic app, in one
#  place: what it gives you, what it costs on each board, and its default.
# ============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE
#   - This file sets DEFAULTS (Zephyr `configdefault`). Flip a default here to
#     change it for every image; to change it for one image, set it in that
#     image's overlay as usual (CONFIG_X=y/n) -- an assignment always wins over
#     a default here.
#   - Anything marked "SET ELSEWHERE" cannot be defaulted from a Kconfig file
#     (it is a member of a Kconfig *choice*, or a board/profile feature); the
#     entry says where it is set.
#   - Debug-only overlays (turn things ON for one build):
#       overlay-threadanalyzer.conf  (already on everywhere; kept for old recipes)
#       overlay-tracing.conf         CTF tracing into an 8 KB RAM buffer
#       overlay-gnsstime.conf        GNSS/1PPS timing lines + bigger log ring
#       overlay-gnssdump.conf        per-satellite NMEA/SNR dump
#       overlay-fault-test.conf      OTA fault-injection timer
#       overlay-coredump-flash.conf  coredump to a flash partition (+ crashtest)
#     Class overlays that switch diagnostics on per fleet class:
#       overlay-health.conf (health report), overlay-rf.conf (rf histograms +
#       path report), overlay-coredump-flash.conf.
#
# COSTS -- the binding budget per board (what running out looks like):
#   Heltec V4 / V4-R8 (ESP32-S3):  internal DRAM `dram0`, 380,672 B.
#                                  Class 4 (V4 member) had 16.0 KB free at 4b9fb8c.
#   XIAO nRF52840:                 flash in the MCUboot app slot, 733,034 B.
#                                  Class 1 had ~17.5 KB free at 4b9fb8c.
#   Numbers are what turning the item OFF gives back ("-") or ON costs ("+"),
#   measured one at a time on the class-4 (V4) and class-1 (XIAO) recipes at
#   main 4b9fb8c (72f5593 for the second batch, [S4]), unless marked [H]
#   (history) or (E) (estimate). Subtract-one
#   deltas do not simply add up. Source tables, method and raw data:
#     ~/lab/dev/zephyrtastic-tooling/docs/scratch/FEATURE-COSTS-AND-ZEPHYR-MODULES.md
#   (the one size reference -- measure a new knob with its sweep script and add
#   the numbers there AND here).
#
# SUMMARY (default | V4 dram0 | XIAO flash) -- biggest first
#   Shell (all of it)          on  | 35.4 KB | 131.9 KB
#   Asserts (ASSERT)           on  | 17.1 KB |  58.6 KB  (strings only, ASSERT_VERBOSE: 11.2 | 37.9)
#   Log text above ERR         on  |  0.5 KB |  56.9 KB  (SET ELSEWHERE: log level choice)
#   Extra exception info (nRF) on  |   -     |  34.3 KB  [S4] -- verify before relying on it
#   Tracing (CTF, RAM buffer)  off | +14.0 KB | +19.3 KB (+12.3 KB RAM)
#   Spinlock validation        on  |  9.4 KB (+9.0 iram) | 13.3 KB   [S4]
#   Thread analyzer (+super-
#     visor, thread summary)   on  |  8.6 KB |   4.0 KB (+8.0 KB RAM)
#   Second UART shell          on  |  7.4 KB |   0 (no uart0 shell on the XIAO)
#   Shell help text            on  |  0 (7.1 KB flash) | 7.7 KB
#   Bootlog                    on  |  0.5 KB |   6.8 KB
#   Supervisor                 on  |  5.0 KB |   1.6 KB (+5.2 KB RAM)
#   Log ring                   on  |  4.2 KB |   2.4 KB (+8.3 KB RAM)
#   Phone log                  on  |  0.8 KB |   2.2 KB
#   Shell log backend          on  |  1.6 KB |   2.1 KB (+1.0 KB RAM)
#   Thread runtime stats       on  |  1.5 KB |   1.6 KB
#   Coredump                   on/XIAO off | 1.2 KB | (sysbuild only)
#   Task watchdog              on/XIAO off | 0.7 KB | -
#   Everything else below is < 1 KB, off, or forced on by something else.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Asserts and fault capture
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# __ASSERT() compiles to nothing unless ASSERT=y. Turns invariant violations
# (e.g. the sx126x DIO1/CAD race class) into a fatal error at the scene instead
# of a symptom three log lines later.
# Cost: -17.1 KB dram0 (-14.6 KB iram, -84 KB flash) on V4 | -58.6 KB XIAO flash.
configdefault ASSERT
	default y

# Keep the checks, drop the file/line/message strings. The single cheapest big
# lever: a failed assert still halts and the coredump still has the PC; only
# the human-readable console line is lost. The operator settled this as the
# DIAGNOSTIC TIER (terse on field images, verbose on bench/dev), not a fleet flag.
# Cost of the strings: -11.2 KB dram0 (-9.4 KB iram) on V4 | -37.9 KB XIAO flash.
configdefault ASSERT_VERBOSE
	default y

# Reboot after a fatal error instead of arch_system_halt() (spin forever with
# IRQs locked -- the "needs a power cycle" outage class). The coredump is taken
# BEFORE the halt-vs-reboot decision (kernel/fatal.c), so nothing forensic is
# lost. A normal warm reset: MCUboot comes back on the same confirmed image.
# (The XIAO board .conf files also set it explicitly, for the fleet's
# revert-on-bad-boot: a hang instead of a reset defeats MCUboot's revert.)
# Cost: ~0.
configdefault RESET_ON_FATAL_ERROR
	default y

# Coredump on a fatal error: registers + all RAM data/bss/noinit (keep
# DEBUG_COREDUMP_MEMORY_DUMP_LINKER_RAM; it is what lets a post-mortem see driver
# statics). Backend SET ELSEWHERE (a choice): LOGGING ("#CD:" log lines, rebuild
# with zephyr/scripts/coredump/coredump_serial_log_parser.py + gdbserver) from
# prj.conf, or FLASH_PARTITION from overlay-coredump-flash.conf (class images).
# XIAO: OFF by default -- the plain (non-sysbuild) XIAO build has no coredump
# partition, and the LOGGING backend spun ~9 s on a dead console until the
# watchdog fired (sometimes landing in the UF2 bootloader). The --sysbuild
# (MCUboot) XIAO image turns it back on in mcuboot-xiao/app.conf, where the
# partition exists.
# Cost: -1.2 KB dram0 on V4 (flash backend) | XIAO: partition on QSPI.
configdefault DEBUG_COREDUMP
	default n if BOARD_XIAO_BLE
	default y

# Xtensa: BREAK before the double-exception vector's `1: j 1b`. Means something
# only with a debugger attached; compiles to nothing otherwise. The fault
# breadcrumbs (EXCCAUSE/EPC1/DEPC/EXCVADDR into RTC memory, `meshtastic resets`)
# are carried patch 0017, CONFIG_XTENSA_FAULT_BREADCRUMBS, a board default.
# Cost: 0. (Exists on ESP32 only.)
configdefault XTENSA_BREAK_ON_UNRECOVERABLE_EXCEPTIONS
	default y

# Stack-overflow detection, the right mechanism per SoC: the MPU guard region on
# nRF52840 (faults at the offending instruction), STACK_SENTINEL on ESP32-S3 (no
# MPU; a magic word checked at context switch -- a fast deep recursion can wedge
# the CPU before it is checked). Also selects STACK_USAGE + INIT_STACKS, which the
# high-water numbers need. Do NOT write CONFIG_STACK_SENTINEL=y anywhere: Kconfig
# silently discards it on boards with an MPU. See src/Kconfig.diagnostics.
# INIT_STACKS, STACK_SENTINEL and the MPU guard are SELECTED by this, so they
# cannot be switched off on their own (tried [S4]: no change).
# Cost: (E) small; the MPU guard costs a region, the sentinel a word per stack.
configdefault MESHTASTIC_STACK_PROTECTION
	default y

# Compiler stack canaries: SET ELSEWHERE -- CONFIG_STACK_CANARIES_STRONG=y in
# prj.conf (a choice; overriding it from the command line did not take, so the
# cost is still unmeasured). STRONG = a canary in every function with a local array or
# an address-taken local. Added after a double exception with healthy
# thread-analyzer numbers 3 minutes earlier (2026-08-08): a canary is checked at
# every return, the analyzer only on a timer.
# Cost: unmeasured (E: a few % of code size).

# nRF: record a fixed-address fault mark a reverted MCUboot test image leaves
# behind (shell: faultmark), for a test image that dies before its console.
# Cost: -0.9 KB XIAO flash [S4]. (nRF52840 only.)
configdefault MESHTASTIC_FAULTMARK
	default y if SOC_NRF52840

# Why the node last rebooted, kept across the reset (`meshtastic resets`).
# Can be turned off since 658863f (the note became a no-op when the trace is
# off, agents-zo3o.7); the hardware lane builds that arm (fleet.c4.no_reboot_trace).
configdefault MESHTASTIC_REBOOT_TRACE
	default y

# Boot log: a record per boot (reason, uptime, version) in RAM, plus a durable
# copy in settings that survives power loss.
# Cost: -0.5 KB dram0 on V4 | -6.8 KB XIAO flash, -0.6 KB RAM (bootlog).
configdefault MESHTASTIC_BOOTLOG
	default y
configdefault MESHTASTIC_BOOTLOG_DURABLE
	default y
# (Durable copy alone: -0.3 KB dram0 on V4 | -1.6 KB XIAO flash [S4].)

# Health report: a periodic compact health message (reboots, RX counts, heap,
# stacks) on a health channel. Class images turn it on with overlay-health.conf.
# Cost: -0.1 KB dram0 on V4 | -0.6 KB XIAO flash.
configdefault MESHTASTIC_HEALTH_REPORT
	default n

# Task watchdog: one channel per subsystem (radio, mesh, workqueue...); a stuck
# subsystem is named in the reset reason instead of a bare hardware WDT.
# XIAO: OFF -- it has no reset button, and its DFU boot guard arms the nRF
# hardware WDT itself (`depends on !WATCHDOG`); MESHTASTIC_DFU_BOOT_GUARD_REQUIRED
# plus a BUILD_ASSERT make turning this on there a build failure, not a silent
# loss of the guard. Operator preference 2026-08-23: no task WDT during XIAO
# bring-up.
# Cost: -0.7 KB dram0 on V4.
configdefault MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG
	default n if BOARD_XIAO_BLE
	default y

# `meshtastic crashtest` (deliberate faults, to prove the coredump path). Class
# images get it with overlay-coredump-flash.conf.
# Cost: -8 B dram0, -0.5 KB flash on V4 [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_SHELL_CRASHTEST
	default n

# OTA fault-injection timer (seconds; 0 = off): overlay-fault-test.conf sets 45.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Stacks, threads, heap, CPU
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# thread_analyzer_run(): per-thread stack high-water + CPU%. The periodic
# REPORTING is ours (MESHTASTIC_THREAD_SUMMARY, 3 threads per line) because
# upstream's THREAD_ANALYZER_AUTO dumped ~58 lines at once and overran the log
# buffer. Caught a real near-miss overflow (STABILITY-2, 2026-08-05).
# Cost (with the supervisor + summary it carries): -8.6 KB dram0 (-1.0 KB iram)
# on V4 | -4.0 KB XIAO flash, -8.0 KB RAM.
configdefault THREAD_ANALYZER
	default y

# Condensed periodic stack%/cpu% summary (needs THREAD_ANALYZER).
# Cost: -0.15 KB dram0 on V4 | -0.5 KB XIAO flash, -0.3 KB RAM [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_THREAD_SUMMARY
	default y

# Supervisor: watches stack headroom, heap floor and CPU hogs, alerts on
# thresholds, and forwards alerts to the phone. Most of its RAM is its alert
# thread's stack. It SELECTS STATS.
# Cost: -5.0 KB dram0 on V4 | -1.6 KB XIAO flash, -5.2 KB RAM [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_SUPERVISOR
	default y
configdefault MESHTASTIC_SUPERVISOR_TO_PHONE
	default y

# sys_heap_runtime_stats_get() (watchdog's periodic heap log, `kernel heap`).
# CANNOT be switched off while MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG is on: meshtastic_watchdog.c
# calls it unguarded, so =n fails to link (found by the cost sweep, 2026-09-26;
# agents-zo3o.7).
# Cost: unmeasurable until the watchdog stops depending on it.
configdefault SYS_HEAP_RUNTIME_STATS
	default y

# Heap allocation tracing (meshtastic_heap_trace.c): every alloc/free logged.
# Floods the log (15% survived last time) -- a one-off tool, off.
# Cost to turn on: +48 B dram0 on V4 | +1.4 KB XIAO flash [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_HEAP_TRACE
	default n

# Power monitor: periodic power-state/current lines. The V4 profile turns it on
# (overlay-v4-unified.conf, SET ELSEWHERE); off elsewhere.
# Cost: -24 B dram0, -0.2 KB flash on V4 [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_POWERMON
	default n

# Kernel tracing (CTF into a RAM buffer): overlay-tracing.conf. Off.
# Cost to turn on: +14.0 KB dram0 (+1.9 KB iram) on V4 | +19.3 KB XIAO flash,
# +12.3 KB RAM [S4]. Would not fit class 4's 16 KB headroom with much to spare.
#
# Thread runtime stats (per-thread CPU cycles; the analyzer's cpu% and the
# supervisor's CPU-hog check need it; Zephyr default, not set here).
# Cost: -1.5 KB dram0 (-1.0 KB iram) on V4 | -1.6 KB XIAO flash, -0.4 KB RAM [S4].
#
# Spinlock validation (SPIN_VALIDATE, a Zephyr default that follows ASSERT):
# checks lock/unlock pairing on every spinlock. Surprisingly large.
# Cost: -9.4 KB dram0 (-9.0 KB iram) on V4 | -13.3 KB XIAO flash, -0.4 KB RAM [S4].
#
# Extra exception info (nRF, EXTRA_EXCEPTION_INFO: a fuller register dump on a
# fault). Measured at -34.3 KB XIAO flash [S4] -- far more than the feature
# itself should cost, so something else probably rides on it; verify before
# trading it away. Exception stack trace (EXCEPTION_STACK_TRACE): -0.2 KB.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Logging
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Levels: CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL (Zephyr modules) is defaulted here; the app's
# own level is a choice, SET ELSEWHERE: MESHTASTIC_LOG_LEVEL_DBG in prj.conf,
# INF in overlay-v4-unified.conf (the Heltec profile).
# Cost of everything above ERR: -0.5 KB dram0 (-26 KB flash) on V4 | -56.9 KB
# XIAO flash (mostly INF/DBG strings and call sites).
configdefault LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL
	default 3

# Deferred-log buffer. Tuned five times; 2048 after "--- N messages dropped ---"
# bursts during the periodic stack summary (2026-08-09).
# Cost: the value itself, in RAM.
configdefault LOG_BUFFER_SIZE
	default 2048

# The log thread formats on its own stack; the ~1 KB Zephyr default overflowed
# at network-up on the V3. overlay-v4-unified.conf sets it again (keep in sync).
# Cost: the value itself, in RAM.
configdefault LOG_PROCESS_THREAD_STACK_SIZE
	default 3072

# Log timestamps as calendar date/time: SET ELSEWHERE (a choice) --
# CONFIG_LOG_OUTPUT_FORMAT_DATE_TIMESTAMP=y in prj.conf.

# Epoch-based log timestamps once the clock is seeded (instead of uptime).
# Cost: -56 B dram0 on V4 | -0.2 KB XIAO flash [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_LOG_WALLCLOCK
	default y

# Log ring: the last ~4 KB of log lines in RAM that survives a warm reset
# (RTC/noinit), read after a crash with `meshtastic logring`. The filter keeps
# chatty modules (powermon, RX lines) from filling its ~3-minute window.
# Cost: -4.2 KB dram0 on V4 (4.3 KB of the 8 KB RTC segment) | -2.4 KB XIAO
# flash, -8.3 KB RAM. Filter: -24 B dram0 on V4 | -0.4 KB XIAO flash [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_LOGRING
	default y
configdefault MESHTASTIC_LOGRING_FILTER
	default y

# Phone log: log records to the app over BLE (LogRecord). Mind the feedback loop
# at DBG (delivering a frame logs, which is another frame).
# Cost: -0.8 KB dram0 on V4 | -2.2 KB XIAO flash.
configdefault MESHTASTIC_PHONELOG
	default y

# Hex dump of every TX/RX packet: the deepest formatter on the log path; can
# overflow the log thread. Wire-level debugging only (raise
# LOG_PROCESS_THREAD_STACK_SIZE with it).
# Cost to turn on: 0 on V4 | +0.6 KB XIAO flash [S4] (plus the stack it needs).
configdefault MESHTASTIC_PACKET_HEXDUMP
	default n

# GNSS timing: `gnsst` lines per NMEA callback (cycle/uptime/UTC/fix) and one
# per 1PPS edge. overlay-gnsstime.conf turns both on (and a 7 KB log ring).
# WARNING: overlay-gnsstime.conf does NOT fit class 4 -- its 7 KB log ring
# overflows the RTC slow segment by 44 B [S4]; use it on a lighter image.
# overlay-gnssdump.conf (per-satellite dump): +1.3 KB dram0, +1.2 KB flash on
# class 4 [S4]. (GNSS images only.)
configdefault MESHTASTIC_GNSS_TIME_DEBUG
	default n
configdefault MESHTASTIC_GNSS_PPS_LOG_EDGES
	default n

# WiFi diagnostics: periodic link snapshots (WiFi images only).
# Cost: (E) ~2 KB (its stack).
configdefault MESHTASTIC_WIFI_DIAG
	default y if WIFI

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Command line and counters
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Meshtastic shell itself (and Zephyr's SHELL under it) is a feature, not a
# default this file sets: images turn it on in their overlays. Cost of all of it
# (stacks + buffers per instance; the command tables are flash): -35.4 KB dram0
# on V4 class 4 | -131.9 KB XIAO flash, -21.3 KB RAM. Zephyr's SHELL cannot be
# switched off while MCUmgr's shell transport is on.

# Second shell on the header UART0 pins (early-boot capture when USB-CDC is
# unreliable). One more shell instance = its own stack and buffers.
# Cost: -7.4 KB dram0 on V4 (the R8 has none) | 0 on the XIAO (no uart0 shell
# node in its devicetree, so the option builds nothing there) [S4].
configdefault MESHTASTIC_SHELL_UART0
	default y

# Shell help strings; the host tool could carry them instead.
# Cost: flash only -- -7.1 KB on V4 | -7.7 KB XIAO [S4] (8.1 KB [H]).
configdefault SHELL_HELP
	default y

# Wildcards in shell commands.
# Cost: -0.1 KB flash on V4 | -2.1 KB XIAO flash [S4].
configdefault SHELL_WILDCARD
	default y

# Named counter groups (`stats list`): task-WDT feed counts, CAD/AGC counters.
# The supervisor selects STATS. MCUmgr's stat and taskstat groups are SET
# ELSEWHERE (overlay-ota-ble.conf; -32 B dram0 on V4 [S4]). STATS itself
# cannot be turned off while the supervisor is on (it selects STATS).
# Cost of the names + shell part: -32 B dram0, -0.5 KB flash on V4 | -0.8 KB
# XIAO flash [S4].
configdefault STATS
	default y
configdefault STATS_NAMES
	default y
configdefault STATS_SHELL
	default y

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Field diagnostics that are features of a class, not defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# rf: RX/TX histograms, `meshtastic rf`, the path report. Class images turn it
# on with overlay-rf.conf.
# Cost: -1.4 KB dram0 on V4 | -10.1 KB XIAO flash, -1.4 KB RAM.
configdefault MESHTASTIC_RF
	default n
